## `story.ni:5190`, stepping out of the clothier's in the gown.

define phrase pieter-wow
  Pieter blinks and does a double take as you step out onto the sidewalk in
  your new finery. 'Wow,' he stammers. 'You look... different. I mean, you
  looked good before, er, with the other dress, I mean, but this is...
  wow.' He blushes, then grins, then shakes his head. 'Come on, Lady Toresal.
  We still have much to do.'
end phrase

## THE STEERING (`story.ni:10804-10819`, `10891-10903`, `8760-8763`): no
## Maiden House, no leaving the square without a gown, no going back to
## Sandler's, no Brothers once the purse is had, no clothier once the gown
## is had, no bakery or butcher, no armory once the dagger is had, no east
## from Commerce Street, no west without a weapon.

define phrase pieter-not-maiden-house
  'No,' says Pieter, pulling you back. 'You'll not be going back to Maiden
  House any time soon. That's exactly where Fossville will expect you to
  go.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-need-a-gown
  'Wait a minute,' Pieter says. 'Dame Sandler said you needed a gown, right?
  We shouldn't leave until you have one.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-dont-bother-sandler
  'There's no need to go back and bother Dame Sandler,' Pieter says. 'We've
  more important things to do.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-done-with-moneylenders
  'We've got what we need from those moneylenders,' Pieter said, 'I'd just as
  soon stay out of their clutches for now.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-already-have-gown
  'You already have your gown,' says Pieter. 'We need to move on.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-not-here-for-food
  'We're not here for food,' Pieter says. 'We have more important things to
  worry about.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-got-your-weapon
  'You've got your weapon already,' Pieter says. 'It's time to move on.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-no-traipsing
  'We don't have time to go traipsing around the city,' says Pieter. 'We
  need to get to Fossville's ball.'
end phrase

define phrase pieter-need-a-weapon
  'Wait a minute,' says Pieter. 'We need to get you a weapon first. We can't
  leave for the ball until you have one.'
end phrase

