## `story.ni:5551-5558`, the letter shown while contemptuous. The source
## then restarts the conversation on CB2 or CB3; here the next `talk to`
## is the loan.

define phrase brothers-read-the-letter
  The brothers both reach out, one with his right hand, the other with his
  left, and delicately take the letter from you. Their eyes flicker back and
  forth in unison as they scan the words. When they reach the end, four
  identical eyebrows shoot up.

  'How very...'

  '...interesting. It would seem you are a personage of more...'

  '...importance than first we assumed.'

  They hand the letter back to you, smiling, and ask in chorus, 'How may we
  help you?'
end phrase

## `story.ni:5563`, shown again.

define phrase brothers-never-forget
  'No need to show us...' begins one brother.

  '...again, Miss,' continues the other. 'We never forget...'

  '...a customer.'
end phrase

## `story.ni:5455`, leaving once they are respectful.

define phrase brothers-come-back-soon
  'Come back soon,' intones one of the brothers as you leave. 'Your business
  is...'

  '...always welcome,' finishes the other.
end phrase

## THE PURSE (`story.ni:5571-5602`) and the gold. It begins nowhere and
## arrives in her hands with the loan; Chapter 10's opening removes it.

create the purse
  aka coin purse, bag, sack, loan, money, gold, small purse, purse of coins, drawstring, drawstrings, string, strings
  a container, openable, starts closed

  The sack is about the size of your fist. It's very heavy. Even a little
  bit of gold goes a long way in Toresal, and there's more than just a
  little bit of gold in here.

  phrase detail while the purse is closed:
    The drawstring is closed.

  phrase detail while the purse is open:
    The drawstring is open.

  after the player opening
    phrase drawstring-pulled-open
  end after

  after the player closing
    phrase drawstring-pulled-closed
  end after

  on the player giving
    refuse purse-very-generous
  end on

  on the player dropping
    refuse purse-unguarded
  end on

  on the player inserting
    refuse purse-unguarded
  end on

define phrase drawstring-pulled-open
  You pull the drawstring open.
end phrase

define phrase drawstring-pulled-closed
  You pull the drawstring closed.
end phrase

define phrase purse-very-generous
  Very generous of you, but you're going to need the money for yourself.
end phrase

define phrase purse-unguarded
  It wouldn't be very wise to leave a bag full of gold coins sitting
  unguarded. Better keep them on your person for now.
end phrase

create the gold coins
  aka coins, coin, gold coin, great seal, seal, seal of the kingdom, kingdom of miradania, miradania, old king, dead king, face
  plural
  in the purse

  Each coin has the Great Seal of the Kingdom of Miradania on one side; the
  face of some old, dead king that you've never heard of on the other.
  You've never seen real gold before, and nothing you've ever seen is quite
  like it. The coins seem to shine with an inner light.

  on the player taking
    refuse coins-stay-in-the-bag
  end on

define phrase coins-stay-in-the-bag
  The bag is the safest place for them, for now. There's no need to take
  them out unless you're planning to purchase something.
end phrase

