## `story.ni:5069`, the clean bell paragraph, once.

define phrase clothier-squeals
  A small bell above the door tinkles as you enter, and a man comes rushing
  out of the store's back room with a measuring cord in his hands, held up
  as though ready to begin fitting you immediately. When he sees that you
  are a clean, respectable, and evidently well-to-do young lady, he
  practically squeals with delight, clapping his hands and plucking at the
  fabric of your clothes with soft, nimble fingers.
end phrase

## His initial appearance by Jack's state (`story.ni:5083`) — room markers
## in the Royal Tunic (GH #364).

define phrase clothier-distaste, stopping while the clothier is here and Jack is not clean
  The clothier stands nearby, eyeing you with some distaste.
end phrase

define phrase clothier-waiting-to-serve, stopping while the clothier is here and Jack is clean
  The clothier hovers nearby, waiting to serve.
end phrase

